@brad2014 thanks for following up on this!
Here is what I found, looking into it a little more. At first, it seems like this PR fixes the issue since the hostname is successfully updated without any errors. However, this is due to the addition of this line https://github.com/hashicorp/vagrant/pull/11877/files#diff-fd473b135e71706459b47b51cb86e249R24 which has a successful output. Since `comm.sudo` is only checking the return code of the last command this appears to works. Removing that line exposes the failure of `find /etc/sysconfig/network-scripts -maxdepth 1 -type f -name 'ifcfg-*' | xargs sed -i 's/\\(DHCP_HOSTNAME=\\).*/\\1\"#{basename}\"/'` which has a return code of `123`. Adding the `-r` argument to `xargs` fixes this. Here is a PR for this https://github.com/hashicorp/vagrant/pull/11910. 
Thanks again for your contribution ❤️
